    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Ambition is the second studio album by American hip hop artist Wale. It was released on November 1, 2011, by Maybach Music Group and Warner Bros. Records. It is the follow-up to his debut album, \"Attention Deficit\", which was released in 2009. The album features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Lloyd, Ne-Yo, Big Sean, Miguel, Meek Mill, Kid Cudi, and Jeremih. The album was supported by five official singles— \"Chain Music\", \"Bait\", Lotus Flower Bomb\", \"Focused\" and \"Sabotage\". \"Ambition\" received generally positive reviews from music critics. The album debuted at number two on the \"Billboard\" 200 chart, selling 164,000 copies in its first week of release. As of June 2013, the album has sold over 482,000 copies in the United States.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
